{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c62d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d602-12a6-7cb3-99d1-8d1cf4fb003f"},"sequence":369,"recorded_at":1780531400000733,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7"},"call_id":"call_01a0d603015e712b9edc1747f535a14a","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/internal/clonereconcile/reconcile.go`.\n1|package clonereconcile\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"sort\"\n5|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonebundle\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonefidelity\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/cloneplan\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonereadback\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// CandidateLink reconciles one captured candidate at tier 1: exactly\n17|// one of Raw (a raw-evidence digest) or Exclusion (a capture class)\n18|// is set. Both set is double-counted; neither set is a missing\n19|// link.\n20|type CandidateLink struct {\n21|\tCandidate string\n22|\tRaw       string\n23|\tExclusion string\n24|}\n25|\n26|// RawLink reconciles one raw item at tier 2: exactly one of\n27|// Canonical (a canonical-object digest) or Normalization (a\n28|// non-synthesized fidelity disposition) is set.\n29|type RawLink struct {\n30|\tRaw           string\n31|\tCanonical     string\n32|\tNormalization string\n33|}\n34|\n35|// History is one sealed staged/live read-back pair: the target\n36|// history ReadBackHistory decoded through the read-back owner. Only\n37|// sealed reads reconcile; the zero value seals nothing and every\n38|// pairing gate refuses it.\n39|type History struct {\n40|\tStaged clonereadback.ValidatedReadBack\n41|\tLive   clonereadback.ValidatedReadBack\n42|}\n43|\n44|// ValidationFields carries the caller-supplied validation-report\n45|// members Reconcile passes to the report owner. The staged/live\n46|// manifest references, the plan/projected references, and the\n47|// fidelity reference are derived by construction from the sealed\n48|// reads and the derived reports, never carried. Valid is decided by\n49|// the owner: the entry attempts true, then false, and exactly one\n50|// seals.\n51|type ValidationFields struct {\n52|\tOperationID                 string\n53|\tProviderManifestID          string\n54|\tExpectedTargetNativeSession string\n55|\tObservedTargetNativeSession string\n56|\tTargetEnvironment           []byte\n57|\tChecks                      clonereadback.ValidationChecks\n58|\tFindings                    []byte\n59|\tExtensions                  map[string]any\n60|\tExpectedFidelityReportID    string\n61|}\n62|\n63|// ReconciliationInput is the caller-supplied reconciliation\n64|// candidate. Candidates with Tier1/Tier2 link it at tiers 1-2;\n65|// Fidelity.Rows links it at tier 3; History pairs target evidence;\n66|// Plan and Projected pair the projection inputs.\n67|type ReconciliationInput struct {\n68|\tCandidates []string\n69|\tTier1      []CandidateLink\n70|\tTier2      []RawLink\n71|\tFidelity   clonefidelity.FidelityReportInput\n72|\tHistory    History\n73|\tPlan       []byte\n74|\tProjected  []byte\n75|\tValidation ValidationFields\n76|}\n77|\n78|// Reconciliation is the proven result: the derived report bytes,\n79|// the owner-decided valid bit, and the tier census counts.\n80|type Reconciliation struct {\n81|\tFidelityReport   []byte\n82|\tFidelityID       string\n83|\tValidationReport []byte\n84|\tValid            bool\n85|\tCandidates       int\n86|\tRawItems         int\n87|\tCanonicalItems   int\n88|\tRows             int\n89|}\n90|\n91|// ReadBackHistory reads back staged and live target history through\n92|// the landed read-back owner: both documents decode via\n93|// clonereadback.DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest under their trusted\n94|// read authorities, and the pair seals only in staged/live order. A\n95|// swapped pair, a relabeled mode, or an authority the purpose does\n96|// not grant refuses; the owner decides every shape, seal, and\n97|// authority rule.\n98|func ReadBackHistory(stagedBytes, liveBytes []byte, stagedAuthority, liveAuthority sessadapter.ReadAuthority) (History, error) {\n99|\tstaged, err := clonereadback.DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest(stagedBytes, stagedAuthority)\n100|\tif err != nil {\n101|\t\treturn History{}, refuse(\"staged read-back invalid: %v\", err)\n102|\t}\n103|\tlive, err := clonereadback.DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest(liveBytes, liveAuthority)\n104|\tif err != nil {\n105|\t\treturn History{}, refuse(\"live read-back invalid: %v\", err)\n106|\t}\n107|\tif err := checkHistoryPair(staged, live); err != nil {\n108|\t\treturn History{}, err\n109|\t}\n110|\treturn History{Staged: staged, Live: live}, nil\n111|}\n112|\n113|// checkHistoryPair enforces that the first sealed read is staged\n114|// and the second is live. The zero value seals nothing: its mode\n115|// reads empty and refuses here before any pairing gate touches it.\n116|func checkHistoryPair(staged, live clonereadback.ValidatedReadBack) error {\n117|\tif staged.Mode() != \"staged\" {\n118|\t\treturn refuse(\"reconciliation staged read is not a staged manifest\")\n119|\t}\n120|\tif live.Mode() != \"live\" {\n121|\t\treturn refuse(\"reconciliation live read is not a live manifest\")\n122|\t}\n123|\treturn nil\n124|}\n125|\n126|// Reconcile proves reconciliation completeness over the three\n127|// tiers and derives both reports through their owners:\n128|//\n129|//   - tier 1: every captured candidate reconciles exactly once to\n130|//     raw evidence or to a capture-class exclusion;\n131|//   - tier 2: every raw item reconciles exactly once to a canonical\n132|//     item or to a non-synthesized normalization disposition;\n133|//   - tier 3: every included candidate and every canonical item\n134|//     occurs in exactly one non-synthesized fidelity row, and every\n135|//     non-loss row resolves staged/live target evidence into the\n136|//     sealed reads while every loss row carries explicit loss with\n137|//     no evidence claim;\n138|//   - pairing: plan, projected manifest, fidelity report, and both\n139|//     reports' tuples bind the same target the reads observe.\n140|//\n141|// The fidelity report seals via clonefidelity, the plan and\n142|// projected inputs decode via cloneplan, and the validation report\n143|// seals via clonereadback, which alone decides the valid bit. Every\n144|// rule is a refusal with a literal code, never a repair.\n145|func Reconcile(input ReconciliationInput) (Reconciliation, error) {\n146|\tif input.Fidelity.Scope != \"target\" {\n147|\t\treturn Reconciliation{}, refuse(\"reconciliation needs a target fidelity report\")\n148|\t}\n149|\tincluded, rawSet, rawByCandidate, err := checkTier1(input.Candidates, input.Tier1)\n150|\tif err != nil {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c62f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d602-12a6-7cb3-99d1-8d1cf4fb003f"},"sequence":370,"recorded_at":1780531400000735,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7"},"call_id":"call_01a0d603035b76098fe3a1d0c276d016","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/internal/clonereconcile/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/clonereconcile\n2|\n3|Final leaf of STORY-260830-21bxa3 (M4): reconciliation completeness\n4|and the Story registry (TASK-260830-1esv6u). This package proves\n5|that every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or\n6|exclusion, every raw item to a canonical item or normalization\n7|disposition, and every canonical item to staged/live target\n8|evidence or a target disposition, by reading back staged/live\n9|target history through the sealed read-back owner and deriving\n10|both reports through their owners.\n11|\n12|Authority quotes below come from\n13|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` (pinned v0.7.0). Line numbers are\n14|1-based.\n15|\n16|## Why this package exists\n17|\n18|Section 13.14.2 states the reconciliation spine (lines\n19|10554-10556) but no landed package owns the cross-tier census:\n20|`clonebundle` owns capture-plan/object reconciliation inside the\n21|Capture Manifest, `clonefidelity` owns row shape and aggregate\n22|reconciliation inside one report, and `clonereadback` owns the\n23|validation report with its sibling-seal and valid rules — while\n24|the read-back leaf explicitly defers tuple cross-match and\n25|plan/projected/fidelity pairing to this final leaf. This package\n26|owns only that composition: the three-tier link census over\n27|caller-projected key sets plus the target-evidence pairing\n28|against sealed reads. It mints no shape, parses no document, and\n29|decides no valid bit of its own.\n30|\n31|## Landed-owner reuse\n32|\n33|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n34||---|---|---|\n35|| Read-back decode | `internal/clonereadback` | `DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest` is the only read path, both modes |\n36|| Validation report + valid bit | `internal/clonereadback` | `BuildValidationReport` (attempted true, then false; exactly one seals) |\n37|| Fidelity rows + report | `internal/clonefidelity` | `BuildFidelityReport`, `DecodeFidelityReport`; tier-3 censuses owner-decoded rows |\n38|| Plan/projected pairing inputs | `internal/cloneplan` | `DecodeProjectionPlan`, `DecodeProjectedObjectManifest` |\n39|| Exclusion vocabulary | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` at every tier-1 exclusion |\n40|| Normalization vocabulary | `internal/clonefidelity` | `ValidDisposition` at every tier-2 normalization |\n41|| Digests | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest` at every raw/canonical/expected digest |\n42|| Tuples | `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` for the validation target tuple |\n43|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at the candidate bound |\n44|\n45|No behavior in any reused package changed: this leaf adds a new\n46|package only and edits no landed file (importer grid below).\n47|\n48|## Axis inventory (written first)\n49|\n50|Every gate axis the conformance matrix walks, with its domain:\n51|\n52|| Axis | Domain | Oracle |\n53||---|---|---|\n54|| A1 capture class | exact, opaque_preserved, excluded, normalized, lost (omitted) per candidate, N 0..6 | class vectors enumerated exhaustively N<=3 (156 sets), sampled N=4..6 (60 vectors per N); each class pins its tier arms and row shape |\n55|| A2 synthesized rows | 0..1 extra rows per cell | synth rows carry no canonical and no captured source evidence; admitted with and without |\n56|| A3 read-back outcome | staged × live in present/absent/mismatched (9 cells) | full 9-cell cross N<=3; nominal + rotated non-nominal N=4..6; claimed evidence must resolve into the read of its side |\n57|| A4 injected tier fault | none + 19 single-break faults (drop/dup/both/neither per tier, double-claims, bad vocabularies, row drops/swaps/strips, ghost/duplicate/malformed keys) | rotating fault per cell; production refusal must name a broken rule (membership); each fault additionally pinned exactly by its gate row |\n58|| A5 validity variant | nominal, flipped check, diverged observed ID, error finding | rotated per cell; valid bit predicted from the spec valid rule, never from production |\n59|| A6 candidate hygiene | UTF-8 validity, 1..512 characters, uniqueness | empty/513/duplicate/invalid-UTF-8 refuse; 512 ASCII and 512 é admit |\n60|| A7 tier-1 arms | raw digest XOR capture-class exclusion per candidate | both/neither/unknown/missing/duplicate refuse; bad digest and bad class refuse |\n61|| A8 tier-2 arms | canonical digest XOR non-synthesized disposition per raw | both/neither/unknown/missing/duplicate refuse; synthesized normalization refuses |\n62|| A9 tier-3 coverage | every included candidate and canonical in exactly one row; rows agree with the tier-1/tier-2 chain | unknown/excluded key, null-vs-named canonical mismatch, unreconciled source evidence, missing row refuse |\n63|| A10 tier-3 evidence | non-loss rows carry ≥1 staged + ≥1 live resolving ID; loss rows carry none | missing side, phantom ID per side, loss-with-evidence refuse |\n64|| A11 pairing | plan/projected IDs, native sessions, tuples, fidelity references across reads and reports | per-side mismatch literals; tuple cross-match both reports |\n65|| A12 valid decision | owner-decided bit over 7 checks, ID equality, findings | true-then-false seal; all four validity shapes seal with the owner bit and decode back |\n66|\n67|Structural arguments. Tiers compose into an injective chain\n68|(I-chain below): tier-1 raw keys are unique, tier-2 canonical\n69|targets are unique, and each tier-3 row agrees with its\n70|candidate's chain, so N<=3 exhausts the link-interaction shapes\n71|(single item, pair interaction, triple interaction) and larger N\n72|adds members but no new shapes; the N=4..6 sample (all-same-class\n73|plus rotating mix) witnesses scale. Read-back outcomes are\n74|independent of capture classes (resolution reads only row claims\n75|against read carries), so the full 9-cell cross runs on the\n76|exhaustive N<=3 corpus. Validity variants are independent of\n77|tiers (the seal step runs last), so rotation covers all four\n78|shapes across the corpus plus the dedicated four-variant test.\n79|\n80|## Interpretation record (decided, pinned)\n81|\n82|Readings taken where the pinned text underdetermines the gate.\n83|Each is pinned by a named test, not prose.\n84|\n85|| # | Reading | Test |\n86||---|---|---|\n87|| I-chain | Each tier link is injective: raw keys unique across tier-1 links and canonical targets unique across tier-2 links. Many-to-one at tier 2 cannot satisfy \"exactly one non-synthesized disposition row\" per canonical with one row per candidate, so it refuses as double-counted. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier1-raw-twice`, `.../tier2-canon-twice` |\n88|| I-loss | The two target dispositions are omitted and unrecoverable (\"explicit loss\"). Loss rows carry empty staged/live sets: evidence plus a loss disposition would reconcile the item twice. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-loss-claims-staged`, `.../tier3-loss-claims-live` |\n89|| I-norm | A normalization disposition is any valid disposition except synthesized: a raw item cannot normalize into a sourceless canonical. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier2-synth-normalization` |\n90|| I-synth | Synthesized rows never claim captured source evidence: their source-evidence IDs are disjoint from the tier-1 raw set. Claimed staged/live IDs still resolve. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-synth-claims` |\n91|| I-resolve | Non-synthesized rows trace to captured source evidence: every source-evidence ID resolves into the tier-1 raw set (the resolution half the fidelity leaf left as a stated bound). | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-unreconciled-evidence` |\n92|| I-order | Candidates need uniqueness, not sortedness: the census sorts internally for determinism. Duplicate declarations refuse. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/candidate-duplicate` |\n93|| I-dupkeys | A second row for one candidate refuses at the fidelity build (owner key uniqueness), wrapped in the reconciliation refusal. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-duplicate-keys-refused-by-owner` |\n94|| I-dupcanon | A second row for one canonical refuses at the agreement gate: tier-2 injectivity makes it disagree with the chain. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-duplicate-canonical-refused-by-agreement` |\n95|| I-canmiss | An uncovered canonical always coincides with an uncovered candidate (one chain, one row), so the candidate census reports the shape. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-missing-row` |\n96|| I-valid | Pairing mismatches refuse (evidence does not belong together); within-report check failures seal with valid=false through the owner. The entry never computes valid: it attempts true, then false. | `TestReconcileValidFollowsOwner` (4 variants) |\n97|| I-scope | Reconciliation is target-only: archive scope refuses before any tier runs. | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/scope-archive` |\n98|\n99|## Clause map (spec sentence → gate → test)\n100|\n101|| # | Pinned clause | Gate | Production site | Test |\n102||---|---|---|---|---|\n103|| C1 | \"Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion\" (10554-10555) | tier-1 census | `checkTier1` | `TestReconciliationProperty` (O1 cells), `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier1-*` (8 rows) |\n104|| C2 | \"every raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition\" (10555) | tier-2 census | `checkTier2` | property (O2 cells), `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier2-*` (10 rows) |\n105|| C3 | \"every canonical item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition\" (10555-10556) | tier-3 census | `checkTier3`, `checkRowEvidenceResolves` | property (O3/O5 cells), `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-*` (16 rows) |\n106|| C4 | \"a synthesized row never claims source evidence\" (derived: synthesized requires no source canonical object; 10602-10603) | synth disjointness | `checkTier3` synth arm | `TestReconcileGateRefusals/tier3-synth-claims`, property synth axis |\n107|| C5 | \"Clone Validation Report 1.0.0 aggregates both reads\" (10581, 10755) | sealed-pair order, sibling references by construction | `checkHistoryPair`, `sealValidationReport` | `TestReadBackHistoryAdmitsSealedPair`, `TestReconcileAdmitsValidTargetHistory` |\n108|| C6 | \"every applicable check must pass\" (10582) + \"valid=true requires every boolean true, matching native IDs/tuple, and no error finding\" (10776-10777) | valid decided by the report owner | `sealValidationReport` (true-then-false) | `TestReconcileValidFollowsOwner`, property (O8 cells) |\n109|| C7 | \"equal expected and observed native Session IDs\" (10741-10742) across reads, plan, projected, and report | native pairing | `checkNativePairing`, `checkValidationNativePairing` | pairing rows (4 literals) |\n110|| C8 | observed/target tuple agreement across reads and both reports (10742, 10768; deferred by the read-back leaf) | tuple cross-match | `checkFidelityPairing`, `checkReportTuplePairing` | pairing rows (3 literals) |\n111|| C9 | plan/projected/fidelity reference pairing (10740-10741, 10760-10765; deferred by the read-back leaf) | digest pairing | `checkPlanPairing`, `checkProjectedPairing`, fidelity binding, expected-fidelity agreement | pairing rows (8 literals) |\n112|| C10 | \"Modes cannot be relabeled\" (10580) | authority-derived modes bind the pair | `ReadBackHistory` via the read-back owner | `TestReadBackHistoryRefusals` |\n113|\n114|## Gate reachability matrix\n115|\n116|Every production refusal site derived mechanically from the\n117|`refuse(\"...\")` call sites (`TestGateReachabilityMatrixDerivedFromRefusalSites`\n118|fails on an unlisted site). Each row breaks only its gate and\n119|asserts its code and detail at the named entry.\n120|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
