cal %q from tier 2\", row.SourceItemKey, want)\n426|\t\t\t}\n427|\t\t\tif row.CanonicalObjectID.String() != want {\n428|\t\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q names canonical %q, tier 2 derives %q\",\n429|\t\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, row.CanonicalObjectID.String(), want)\n430|\t\t\t}\n431|\t\t} else if row.CanonicalObjectID != nil {\n432|\t\t\t// normalized[raw] holds here by tier-2 closure: the raw\n433|\t\t\t// took the normalization arm, so the row must carry a\n434|\t\t\t// null canonical.\n435|\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q names canonical %q under normalization\",\n436|\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, row.CanonicalObjectID.String())\n437|\t\t}\n438|\t\tfor _, evidence := range row.SourceEvidenceIDs {\n439|\t\t\tif !rawSet[evidence.String()] {\n440|\t\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q claims unreconciled source evidence %q\", row.SourceItemKey, evidence.String())\n441|\t\t\t}\n442|\t\t}\n443|\t\tif isLossDisposition(row.Disposition) {\n444|\t\t\tif len(row.StagedEvidenceObjectIDs) > 0 {\n445|\t\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 loss row %q claims staged evidence %q\",\n446|\t\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, row.StagedEvidenceObjectIDs[0].String())\n447|\t\t\t}\n448|\t\t\tif len(row.LiveEvidenceObjectIDs) > 0 {\n449|\t\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 loss row %q claims live evidence %q\",\n450|\t\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, row.LiveEvidenceObjectIDs[0].String())\n451|\t\t\t}\n452|\t\t\tcontinue\n453|\t\t}\n454|\t\tif len(row.StagedEvidenceObjectIDs) == 0 {\n455|\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q has no staged target evidence\", row.SourceItemKey)\n456|\t\t}\n457|\t\tif len(row.LiveEvidenceObjectIDs) == 0 {\n458|\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q has no live target evidence\", row.SourceItemKey)\n459|\t\t}\n460|\t\tif err := checkRowEvidenceResolves(row, stagedBlobs, liveBlobs); err != nil {\n461|\t\t\treturn err\n462|\t\t}\n463|\t}\n464|\t// Every canonical belongs to exactly one candidate's chain\n465|\t// by tier-2 injectivity, and each present row's canonical\n466|\t// agrees with its candidate's chain, so an uncovered\n467|\t// canonical always coincides with an uncovered candidate and\n468|\t// the candidate census below reports the shape.\n469|\tvar missingCandidates []string\n470|\tfor candidate := range included {\n471|\t\tif !coveredCandidates[candidate] {\n472|\t\t\tmissingCandidates = append(missingCandidates, candidate)\n473|\t\t}\n474|\t}\n475|\tsort.Strings(missingCandidates)\n476|\tif len(missingCandidates) > 0 {\n477|\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 candidate %q has no disposition row\", missingCandidates[0])\n478|\t}\n479|\treturn nil\n480|}\n481|\n482|// checkRowEvidenceResolves enforces that every evidence ID a row\n483|// claims resolves into the sealed read of its side: staged IDs\n484|// into staged blob IDs, live IDs into live blob IDs. Absent or\n485|// mismatched read-back refuses with the side and the phantom ID.\n486|func checkRowEvidenceResolves(\n487|\trow clonefidelity.DispositionRecord,\n488|\tstagedBlobs, liveBlobs map[string]bool,\n489|) error {\n490|\tfor _, evidence := range row.StagedEvidenceObjectIDs {\n491|\t\tif !stagedBlobs[evidence.String()] {\n492|\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q claims staged evidence %q outside the staged read\",\n493|\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, evidence.String())\n494|\t\t}\n495|\t}\n496|\tfor _, evidence := range row.LiveEvidenceObjectIDs {\n497|\t\tif !liveBlobs[evidence.String()] {\n498|\t\t\treturn refuse(\"tier-3 row %q claims live evidence %q outside the live read\",\n499|\t\t\t\trow.SourceItemKey, evidence.String())\n500|\t\t}\n501|\t}\n502|\treturn nil\n503|}\n504|\n505|// checkPlanPairing enforces that both sealed reads name the decoded\n506|// projection plan: the reads aggregate the plan Reconcile pairs,\n507|// never a neighbor.\n508|func checkPlanPairing(history History, plan cloneplan.ProjectionPlan) error {\n509|\tif history.Staged.Manifest().ProjectionPlanID != plan.PlanID {\n510|\t\treturn refuse(\"staged read names projection plan %q, want %q\",\n511|\t\t\thistory.Staged.Manifest().ProjectionPlanID.String(), plan.PlanID.String())\n512|\t}\n513|\tif history.Live.Manifest().ProjectionPlanID != plan.PlanID {\n514|\t\treturn refuse(\"live read names projection plan %q, want %q\",\n515|\t\t\thistory.Live.Manifest().ProjectionPlanID.String(), plan.PlanID.String())\n516|\t}\n517|\treturn nil\n518|}\n519|\n520|// checkProjectedPairing enforces that both sealed reads name the\n521|// decoded projected object manifest.\n522|func checkProjectedPairing(history History, projected cloneplan.ProjectedManifest) error {\n523|\tif history.Staged.Manifest().ProjectedObjectManifestID != projected.ManifestID {\n524|\t\treturn refuse(\"staged read names projected manifest %q, want %q\",\n525|\t\t\thistory.Staged.Manifest().ProjectedObjectManifestID.String(), projected.ManifestID.String())\n526|\t}\n527|\tif history.Live.Manifest().ProjectedObjectManifestID != projected.ManifestID {\n528|\t\treturn refuse(\"live read names projected manifest %q, want %q\",\n529|\t\t\thistory.Live.Manifest().ProjectedObjectManifestID.String(), projected.ManifestID.String())\n530|\t}\n531|\treturn nil\n532|}\n533|\n534|// checkNativePairing enforces that both reads observe the same\n535|// target native session and the decoded plan and projected manifest\n536|// expect it: one target across all four documents.\n537|func checkNativePairing(history History, plan cloneplan.ProjectionPlan, projected cloneplan.ProjectedManifest) error {\n538|\tstaged := history.Staged.Manifest()\n539|\tlive := history.Live.Manifest()\n540|\tif staged.ObservedTargetNativeSession != live.ObservedTargetNativeSession {\n541|\t\treturn refuse(\"staged and live reads observe different native sessions\")\n542|\t}\n543|\tif plan.ExpectedTargetNativeSession != staged.ObservedTargetNativeSession {\n544|\t\treturn refuse(\"projection plan expects native session %q, reads observe %q\",\n545|\t\t\tplan.ExpectedTargetNativeSession, staged.ObservedTargetNativeSession)\n546|\t}\n547|\tif projected.ExpectedTargetNativeSession != staged.ObservedTargetNativeSession {\n548|\t\treturn refuse(\"projected manifest expects native session %q, reads observe %q\",\n549|\t\t\tprojected.ExpectedTargetNativeSession, staged.ObservedTargetNativeSession)\n550|\t}\n551|\treturn nil\n552|}\n553|\n554|// checkFidelityPairing enforces that the derived fidelity report\n555|// binds the sealed reads it reconciles: its staged/live manifest\n556|// references name the reads, and its target tuple equals both\n557|// observed tuples.\n558|func checkFidelityPairing(history History, fidelity clonefidelity.FidelityReport) error {\n559|\tif fidelity.StagedReadBackEvidenceManifestID == nil ||\n560|\t\t*fidelity.StagedReadBackEvidenceManifestID != history.Staged.ManifestID() {\n561|\t\treturn refuse(\"fidelity report does not bind the staged read\")\n562|\t}\n563|\tif fidelity.LiveReadBackEvidenceManifestID == nil ||\n564|\t\t*fidelity.LiveReadBackEvidenceManifestID != history.Live.ManifestID() {\n565|\t\treturn refuse(\"fidelity report does not bind the live read\")\n566|\t}\n567|\t// A target-scope report always carries a target tuple by the\n568|\t// owner's branch-exact seal, so the dereference below is\n569|\t// total on decoded target reports.\n570|\tif *fidelity.TargetEnvironment != history.Staged.Manifest().ObservedEnvironment {\n571|\t\treturn refuse(\"fidelity target tuple differs from the staged observed tuple\")\n572|\t}\n573|\tif *fidelity.TargetEnvironment != history.Live.Manifest().ObservedEnvironment {\n574|\t\treturn refuse(\"fidelity target tuple differs from the live observed tuple\")\n575|\t}\n576|\treturn nil\n577|}\n578|\n579|// checkReportTuplePairing enforces the validation report's\n580|// target-tuple cross-match: the report tuple equals the staged\n581|// observed tuple. The live side needs no second site: fidelity\n582|// pairing already proved both observed tuples equal the fidelity\n583|// target, so equality with staged is equality with live.\n584|func checkReportTuplePairing(history History, target sessadapter.Tuple) error {\n585|\tif target != history.Staged.Manifest().ObservedEnvironment {\n586|\t\treturn refuse(\"validation target tuple differs from the staged observed tuple\")\n587|\t}\n588|\treturn nil\n589|}\n590|\n591|// checkValidationNativePairing enforces that the validation report\n592|// is about the observed target: its expected native session equals\n593|// the reads' observed session. The expected/observed equality\n594|// inside the report stays the owner's valid rule.\n595|func checkValidationNativePairing(history History, expected string) error {\n596|\tif expected != history.Staged.Manifest().ObservedTargetNativeSession {\n597|\t\treturn refuse(\"validation report expects native session %q, reads observe %q\",\n598|\t\t\texpected, history.Staged.Manifest().ObservedTargetNativeSession)\n599|\t}\n600|\treturn nil\n601|}\n602|\n603|// sealValidationReport derives the validation report through the\n604|// read-back owner: references bind the sealed siblings and the\n605|// derived reports by construction, and the valid bit is decided by\n606|// the owner alone. The entry attempts true, then false; exactly one\n607|// seals, because the owner refuses any claimed bit that disagrees\n608|// with its decision.\n609|func sealValidationReport(input ReconciliationInput, fidelity clonefidelity.FidelityReport) ([]byte, bool, error) {\n610|\towner := clonereadback.ValidationReportInput{\n611|\t\tOperationID:                      input.Validation.OperationID,\n612|\t\tProjectionPlanID:                 input.History.Staged.Manifest().ProjectionPlanID.String(),\n613|\t\tProjectedObjectManifestID:        input.History.Staged.Manifest().ProjectedObjectManifestID.String(),\n614|\t\tStagedReadBackEvidenceManifestID: input.History.Staged.ManifestID().String(),\n615|\t\tLiveReadBackEvidenceManifestID:   input.History.Live.ManifestID().String(),\n616|\t\tTargetProviderManifestID:         input.Validation.ProviderManifestID,\n617|\t\tFidelityReportID:                 fidelity.ReportID.String(),\n618|\t\tExpectedTargetNativeSession:      input.Validation.ExpectedTargetNativeSession,\n619|\t\tObservedTargetNativeSession:      input.Validation.ObservedTargetNativeSession,\n620|\t\tTargetEnvironment:                input.Validation.TargetEnvironment,\n621|\t\tStagedStructuralValid:            input.Validation.Checks.StagedStructuralValid,\n622|\t\tLiveStructuralValid:              input.Validation.Checks.LiveStructuralValid,\n623|\t\tSemanticMarkerValid:              input.Validation.Checks.SemanticMarkerValid,\n624|\t\tIdentityValid:                    input.Validation.Checks.IdentityValid,\n625|\t\tWorkspaceBindingValid:            input.Validation.Checks.WorkspaceBindingValid,\n626|\t\tResumeSurfaceValid:               input.Validation.Checks.ResumeSurfaceValid,\n627|\t\tSourceGenerationRevalidated:      input.Validation.Checks.SourceGenerationRevalidated,\n628|\t\tFindings:                         input.Validation.Findings,\n629|\t\tExtensions:                       input.Validation.Extensions,\n630|\t}\n631|\towner.Valid = true\n632|\tsealed, err := clonereadback.BuildValidationReport(owner, input.History.Staged, input.History.Live)\n633|\tif err == nil {\n634|\t\treturn sealed, true, nil\n635|\t}\n636|\towner.Valid = false\n637|\tsealed, retryErr := clonereadback.BuildValidationReport(owner, input.History.Staged, input.History.Live)\n638|\tif retryErr == nil {\n639|\t\treturn sealed, false, nil\n640|\t}\n641|\treturn nil, false, refuse(\"validation report invalid: %v; %v\", err, retryErr)\n642|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
