{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c881","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d602-12a6-7cb3-99d1-8d1cf4fb003f"},"sequence":667,"recorded_at":1780531400001329,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d604-c913-7cb1-8fd0-15283983af82"},"task_id":"01a0d604-c913-7cb1-8fd0-15283983af82","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d604-c913-7cb1-8fd0-15283983af82","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/internal/clonereconcile/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/clonereconcile.\n3|\n4|Every decision gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n5|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n6|reject, and the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant\n7|proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through a production entry), V (verdict from the Go\n11|exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\n12|failure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else --\n13|unapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\n14|infrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file\n15|is restored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\n16|\n17|The four T- rows are token-preserving attacks: the searched-for\n18|token still matches, but the decision changes. Their killers execute\n19|the behavioral gate tests, and the full package suite re-runs on all\n20|four to prove the always-on suite kills them too.\n21|\n22|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n23|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n24|hard-coding kills.\n25|\n26|The two fidelity-report wrap sites carry no mutant: they forward the\n27|owner's refusal and any weakening still refuses with the identical\n28|literal (the decode fallback), so no verdict change is expressible.\n29|They are covered by the owner suite plus the wrap tests.\n30|\n31|Digests embedded below are deterministic fixture outputs (sha256 over\n32|fixed seeds); a fixture change fails the patch application loudly\n33|instead of silently testing a new member.\n34|\n35|Usage:\n36|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonereconcile/testdata/mutant_harness.py [--log-dir DIR] [MUTANT ...]\n37|\"\"\"\n38|\n39|import shutil\n40|import subprocess\n41|import sys\n42|import time\n43|from dataclasses import dataclass\n44|from pathlib import Path\n45|\n46|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n47|PACKAGE = \"internal/clonereconcile\"\n48|TARGET = \"internal/clonereconcile/reconcile.go\"\n49|\n50|RAW0 = \"sha256:f85d70a61f8936e59753518dec2603666dbbc943722bff045c0a6011be08aeb5\"\n51|RAW2 = \"sha256:feeb74ff2b27e5e4d20e2a4b317ae44fce85548205fa92ffa06de1ebc344a49b\"\n52|CANON0 = \"sha256:fbdd0b01d4b38469a7161da02b326942a6b537a3169078b02b70c2d011533f80\"\n53|CANON1 = \"sha256:c2e2abc08246be4c6057dbdd134bfa04ba65f2bd9d81eafe2073fa61a1c4c764\"\n54|PHANTOM = \"sha256:799ac6577a0b2d6da214bd9d12ae1d5febf1e22e3f610f5b82a9cb2237acab3a\"\n55|STAGED0 = \"sha256:6e7236396050a92937998fd5bb9b2d63dca651d76fe49089f0a38f555d24ca9b\"\n56|LIVE0 = \"sha256:301d60fd5c4d5f982d2a2dc9059b6f1b1c50f76de48376aa537183cc0b13505f\"\n57|PLANA = \"sha256:d97c95b798668173a1dcd2203b6f646c9bef874ed56eb0558afa8da78da92bd9\"\n58|PLANB = \"sha256:a4b35f9d23736760bcef679ffcd31176a59f8628edb8394a5c8de8e4fb82f642\"\n59|PROJA = \"sha256:eba510d8697301f2ef1f62eaab26d80f07ef61ebedc6595034cb1beddd77202f\"\n60|PROJB = \"sha256:ee806e83