{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3ff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d602-12a6-7cb3-99d1-8d1cf4fb003f"},"sequence":2138,"recorded_at":1780531400004271,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8384434d-9d62-45ba-bafd-be548807fde7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d61d-f20a-7bd1-8b05-61e105fb7ea2"},"task_id":"01a0d61d-f20a-7bd1-8b05-61e105fb7ea2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d61d-f20a-7bd1-8b05-61e105fb7ea2","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-24\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-1esv6u — story-final reconciliation completeness and registry\n9|\n10|- PRODUCER: New `internal/clonereconcile` proves SPEC v0.7.0 §13.14.2 reconciliation completeness (10554-10556) through two entries: `ReadBackHistory` decodes staged/live history solely via `clonereadback.DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest`, and `Reconcile` censuses tier-1/tier-2 links, owner-decoded fidelity rows at tier 3, and plan/projected/tuple/native pairing, then derives both reports through `clonefidelity`/`cloneplan`/`clonereadback` with the owner-decided valid bit (true-then-false seal).\n11|- PROPERTY: `TestReconciliationProperty` (2,808 cells: N≤3 class vectors × synth counts × 9 read-back outcomes × rotating faults × rotating validity) plus `TestReconciliationPropertyLargeN` (720 cells, N=4..6) run the production entry against an independent oracle; refusal asserts membership over the broken-rule set, admission asserts the oracle valid bit.\n12|- GATES: 65-row `TestReconcileGateRefusals` pins every refusal literal exactly; entry/owner-reachability census plus the no-reimplementation guard (both control-planted), skip census (empty allowlist), and the mechanical refusal-site→matrix census are green. Five unreachable-by-construction sites were removed during test design (owner-shadowed duplicates, tier-closure canonical census, owner-guaranteed tuple presence) so every listed site stays breakable.\n13|- MUTANTS: 63-row harness: 58 narrowings killed alone, 4 token-preserving attacks killed alone and under the full suite, 1 applied neutral control survived; zero ERROR rows. The two fidelity-report forwarding wraps carry no mutant (any weakening refuses identically); documented in TRACEABILITY.\n14|- REGISTRY: Story-final edit adds five leaf cases and the `section:13.14.2` unmeasured binding (0 scanner clauses, 13.14.5 precedent; no 13.14.4 binding — no implementation in the story). Digest re-derived to `ab7b66cc6d85df8ed7eac2aa5cd7b7fa635db20a3e5092824490b435f94ed3f1`; tracecheck prints `bindings=73 ... unmeasured=5 ... 168 cases`; README ownership paragraph, measured-coverage fenced line, and all pin tests updated at five sites.\n15|- VALIDATION: Full `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (51/51 packages); importer owner suites green; `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0; gofmt clean; clonereconcile coverage 99.2%; scratch-index tree is exactly 8 modified + 12 new files. Candidate left uncommitted. AC ratio 6 of 6 rows driven (crash/idempotency vacuous-with-proof: pure entries, determinism+purity tests).\n16|\n17|### TASK-260830-2h5uv9 rev5 — always-on common-ID position product\n18|\n19|- The configured generated sync test now runs its N≤3 bounded shard without a selector. A separate always-on 432-case production `DurableIndex.SyncFrom` product places a same-identity/different-bytes conflict at each of three sorted common-ID positions, crossed with all six arrival permutations, duplicate on/off, both skews, rounds 1–3, and two peer-only lease identities. It asserts literal `integrity_failure`, quarantine bytes, peer immutability, and conflict on retry.\n20|- Added AST skip census (zero unallowlisted skips), ordinary and token-preserving planted-skip refusals, and repository-root `.pyc`/`__pycache__` hygiene plus planted-artifact refusal. Removed the task-owned scratch Python cache; the focused selected tests and determinism run are green.\n21|- The four review narrowings—first namespace, first ID, last ID, even IDs only—are killed alone by `TestDurableSyncConflictAuditsEveryCommonIDPositionWithPeerOnlyRecord`; each rework plant was run in a targeted invocation and in the 86-row shipped harness. The token-preserving skip plant is killed by `TestSkipCensusRejectsAnUnjustifiedPlantedSkip`. The applied neutral comment control survives. Harness results: 85 kills, one control survivor, zero invalid rows.\n22|- Registry decode confirms all three Story acceptance cases occur in their declared clause bindings and names `SyncFrom` production ownership; digest re-derives to `2302a10a0174ada997614ea7d6112add30e9b2328f6b25ea796ea175f48568cd`. Tracecheck is green; README pin passes and the wrong-figure plant fails. Scoped diagnostics refuse at §5.3 (7/8), §10.7 (1/18), and §11.4 (6/7), as expected for the stated task boundary.\n23|- Exact `go list -test -json` comparison: fork base `0ca3e4c` to candidate is 44→46 package paths, 1,468→1,592 references, and 317→350 internal references; tracked target importer union is 25→27 with no removed target edges. New target callers are `merkleinventory` for canonicaljson/rpcwire and test-only `tmuxserver` for provhost. Base importer execution is reused from its immutable green evidence; all 27 candidate importers are in the exact candidate suite.\n24|- Focused package gate, final `-count=3` determinism gate, exact full configured suite (46/46 packages), Windows vet, gofmt, build, tracecheck, scratch-index diff check, and `task-board.config.json` byte comparison all have green evidence after the repository-root bytecode hygiene change. The final full suite and determinism process exited 0; raw output is attached and read back.\n25|- Measured task acceptance ratio remains 1 of 2 criteria fully driven by named tests; the no-public-capability clause is a stated scope bound because this internal library adds no public advertisement entry point. The producer brief has no formal surface table; `coverage-map.md` records this as a brief gap. Candidate remains uncommitted at the Story checkpoint; current origin main is still `6d3bff9`.\n26|\n27|### TASK-260830-2h5uv9 rev4 — partial-overlap conflict crossed with generated sync product\n28|\n29|- Rework adds generated same-ID/different-bytes cases beside peer-only identities across reorder, duplicate, gap-fill, both clock skews, partial peer, and rounds 1–3. The review reproduction is named in `TestDurableSyncConflictWithPartialOverlapPeer`; an AST check guards unconditional common-ID audit. Product audit: 38,000 valid + 37,765 conflict cases; N1–N5 full, N6 34 samples. All successful selector ranges are attached; two wide N6 selectors timed out and were rerun successfully in smaller non-overlapping selectors.\n30|- Validation on this candidate: full `go test ./... -count=1`, Windows vet, build, diff check, tracecheck, determinism `-count=3`, and README coverage pin all exit 0. Wrong README figure plant exits 1 as expected. Mutation harness: 83 rows, 81 narrowing kills, one token-preserving behavior kill, one applied neutral control survivor; no NOT_APPLIED rows. Registry digest `cf559de0d70bf68546b12169ff30549022d106939d9dab71ac691fa260b34c80`.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
